			// attrs will be added after content if content exists? Original order: +content first then attrs in yaml output for <root a="1">text</root> (content before attr despite attr known first). They buffer content and when finishing decide order.
			// store attrs in frame temporarily in node but we'll rebuild order at end: collect attrs separately
			// Simplify: add attrs to a temp map stored in fr.node as placeholder: we'll add directly and reorder at EndElement if content present.
			for _,at:=range t.Attr{
				fr.hasAttrs=true
